        "id": "tool:answer-questions-about-many-states",
        "label": "Answer the same questions about many states, in bulk, on this Mac",
        "job": "Ask the same set of questions about every one of these lines or records, all at once, with my classifier model",
        "description": "Takes the model's value, the question set, the settings and the states in the request, and asks every state every question on this Mac: the questions run once as a cached prefix and the states batched against them on Apple's GPU through MLX. The answer for each state and question is the classifier's probabilities over its options (choice: each option; score: each level, with the expected level; noul: the probability of yes). The answer returns them all: {status, states_done, states, classifier_answers_as, seconds, answers: [{index, id?, answers: {question id: answer}}]}. The caller reads the inputs from the person's lists and puts the answers wherever it wants them; nothing is written to the person's records, and nothing is kept on this Mac: the states go to the classifier program on a pipe and its answers come back on one.",
